<ontology/use_leather_tanning/use_leather_tanning__0132__q3/#resource> dcterms:bibliographicCitation "Simmonds (1892), Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products, scan p. 274" ;
    dcterms:source <https://archive.org/details/b21780535/page/n274/mode/1up> ;
    a <ontology/EvidenceQuote/#resource> ;
    rdfs:label "Evidence for Valonia used in Leather Tanning, Tawing & Currying: Simmonds (1892), Commercial Dictionary of Trade Products, scan p. 274"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "Under the heads of Cork, Quercitron, and Valonia, other products of oak will be found noticed. OAK-BARK, the bark of the oak which is largely used for tanning; the inner cortical of young trees being preferred, as containing a larger proportion of tannin."@en ;
    <ontology/retrievalMode/#resource> "direct_sentence" .
